WEBVTT

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.936
Last time
on Star Trek: Voyager...

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:08.202
Chakotay, they're going
to take your son.

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.970
When Culluh saw the baby
wasn't his...

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:13.411
Please, Chakotay, help us...
not for me, for your son.

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.573
I told you to stay out of here.

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:16.809
No!

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.715
I have a duty to this crew.

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:21.585
I can't just leave
and go looking for the child.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.179
And I'd never consider
letting you go

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:25.157
into a Kazon-Nistrim
stronghold by yourself.

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.992
Captain, if I can get a shuttle
through the crossfire,

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.327
I can go back

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.355
and bring the Talaxians
to help us.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:51.911
We're being boarded through
the shuttle bays, Captain.

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:52.918
Stay where you are!

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:53.941
Don't move!

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:58.889
Hold your fire.

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:01.325
Computer, activate
medical holographic recall.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:02.692
Set for 12 hours.
Mark.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.596
A fitting end for a people

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.897
who would not share
their technology.

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:11.665
Let's see if you manage
to survive...

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.865
without it.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:16.137
We'll divide the crew
into teams.

00:01:16.176 --> 00:01:18.110
Each of you will be
a team leader.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:20.738
Make it clear to all your people
that we expect to be rescued.

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:25.374
And now, the conclusion.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.103
Let me help you.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:46.366
No, really, I'm all right.

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:47.873
Don't push yourself.

00:01:47.907 --> 00:01:49.465
That goes for everyone.

00:01:49.509 --> 00:01:51.477
Perspiring wastes water.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.658
All right, people, follow me.

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.823
Let's take it slow.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:38.757
This is the most defensible
location we've seen so far.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.850
The overhang should
provide us with shelter,

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:43.294
and the breeze
should keep insects away.

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:45.695
All right, let's make camp.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:58.173
Neelix, look at this.

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:00.202
They almost look constructed.

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:03.306
Maybe the people on this world
are cave dwellers.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.283
If that's true,

00:03:05.318 --> 00:03:07.946
I'd say this is
a "do not disturb" sign.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.477
Wouldn't you?

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:11.547
They look humanoid.

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:15.493
We might be able to use these
as tools or weapons.

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:17.519
Gather them up, Mr. Hogan.

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:20.727
Is there a problem?

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:23.167
No, sir.

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:25.330
Do you want all of them?

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:26.963
Waste nothing.

00:03:27.073 --> 00:03:29.371
That's one of the first rules
of survival.

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:31.070
Neelix, over here!

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:05.633
Hogan!

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:03.293
Computer,
repeat stabilizer diagnostic.

00:06:03.329 --> 00:06:04.353
Damage has been detected

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:07.264
in the stabilizer
acceleration sensors.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.928
I just repaired
the acceleration sensors.

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:14.666
Warning. Vessel approaching
on intercept course.

00:06:14.707 --> 00:06:16.106
Signature.

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.905
Kazon patrol vessel.

00:06:19.779 --> 00:06:21.872
Damn it, I don't
have time for this.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:32.680
I don't have time for this!

00:06:32.725 --> 00:06:35.057
Computer, all stop.

00:06:40.466 --> 00:06:42.593
Engage impulse.

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.341
Told you,
I don't have time for this.

00:06:57.617 --> 00:06:59.949
It's all that left
of Hogan's uniform, Captain.

00:06:59.986 --> 00:07:02.045
We didn't find anything else.

00:07:09.028 --> 00:07:11.519
This is my fault.

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:13.896
If I hadn't told Hogan
to pick up those bones...

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:15.366
You shouldn't blame
yourself, Neelix.

00:07:15.401 --> 00:07:16.368
Stop it.

00:07:16.402 --> 00:07:18.267
There's no time
to worry about blame.

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:20.568
Hogan was a fine officer
and a good man.

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:22.631
And our job is
to make sure his death

00:07:22.675 --> 00:07:24.506
is the last one for a long time.

00:07:24.544 --> 00:07:27.240
I will not let this planet
destroy my crew.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.679
Kes, see to it
that everyone knows

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:30.579
the tunnels are off limits.

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:32.243
I want clear safety
protocols established.

00:07:32.285 --> 00:07:33.616
Mr. Tuvok, we need weapons.

00:07:33.653 --> 00:07:34.779
I have already begun to design

00:07:34.821 --> 00:07:36.118
some rudimentary devices,
Captain.

00:07:36.155 --> 00:07:37.486
What's our food
and water status?

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:39.150
I know it sounds grisly,

00:07:39.192 --> 00:07:40.386
but I can make solar stills

00:07:40.426 --> 00:07:41.950
with the material
from this uniform.

00:07:42.028 --> 00:07:43.290
We could have water tomorrow.

00:07:43.329 --> 00:07:45.320
Do it.

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:47.628
Captain,
none of the search teams

00:07:47.667 --> 00:07:50.135
were able to find plants
of any nutritional value.

00:07:52.371 --> 00:07:55.033
Then tell the crew to start
turning over rocks.

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:04.374
If anyone balks at eating these,

00:08:04.417 --> 00:08:06.146
tell them it's an order
from their Captain.

00:08:06.185 --> 00:08:08.483
They may be the difference
between life and death.

00:08:19.899 --> 00:08:23.027
Activate emergency medical
holographic program.

00:08:23.069 --> 00:08:26.402
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:29.135
Hello, Doctor.
Remember me?

00:08:29.175 --> 00:08:31.837
How could I forget such an
intriguing medical mystery?

00:08:31.878 --> 00:08:33.212
A Bajoran crewman with
a Cardassian physiology.

00:08:33.212 --> 00:08:34.304
A Bajoran crewman with
a Cardassian physiology.

00:08:34.346 --> 00:08:35.813
How are you, Seska?

00:08:36.848 --> 00:08:38.372
I see we have a new passenger.

00:08:38.417 --> 00:08:42.478
Doctor, I have to inform you
about a change of command.

00:08:42.521 --> 00:08:44.512
I'm curious how you'll react.

00:08:44.556 --> 00:08:47.389
The Kazon-Nistrim
have taken Voyager.

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:48.654
How interesting.

00:08:48.694 --> 00:08:50.821
Does your program have
any problem with that?

00:08:50.862 --> 00:08:52.955
One humanoid is pretty
much the same as another

00:08:53.031 --> 00:08:54.521
from a holographic
point of view.

00:08:54.566 --> 00:08:57.126
I'm programmed
to provide medical care

00:08:57.169 --> 00:08:58.830
to anyone who needs it.

00:08:59.838 --> 00:09:01.772
Tell me, is it
within your program's

00:09:01.807 --> 00:09:04.708
capabilities to lie
or be deceptive?

00:09:04.743 --> 00:09:06.267
I've learned
that a bedside manner

00:09:06.311 --> 00:09:08.302
occasionally requires me to...

00:09:08.347 --> 00:09:09.507
how shall I put it?...

00:09:09.548 --> 00:09:11.812
soft-pedal the truth.

00:09:11.850 --> 00:09:15.149
But bald-faced lying,
calculated deceit... I don't have

00:09:15.187 --> 00:09:17.087
much experience
with that sort of thing.

00:09:17.122 --> 00:09:19.249
But my program is adaptive.

00:09:19.291 --> 00:09:21.259
If you really need me
to be deceptive,

00:09:21.293 --> 00:09:22.521
I'm sure I could learn.

00:09:22.561 --> 00:09:24.358
That's not exactly what I meant.

00:09:24.396 --> 00:09:26.387
I think we'll keep you
just as you are.

00:09:26.431 --> 00:09:27.523
As you wish.

00:09:27.566 --> 00:09:28.828
Your baby's in good health.

00:09:28.867 --> 00:09:32.598
Oh, you don't know
how primitive Kazon medicine is.

00:09:32.638 --> 00:09:34.333
I'm sure Chakotay
would be glad to know

00:09:34.373 --> 00:09:36.034
you're looking after his son.

00:09:36.074 --> 00:09:37.507
Chakotay's son?

00:09:37.542 --> 00:09:39.442
That isn't Chakotay's son.

00:09:39.478 --> 00:09:41.105
But you're wrong, Doctor.

00:09:41.146 --> 00:09:44.582
I impregnated myself
with his DNA.

00:09:44.616 --> 00:09:46.948
That may have been
your intention...

00:09:47.019 --> 00:09:49.920
but it certainly
wasn't the result.

00:09:49.955 --> 00:09:51.513
Here.

00:09:51.556 --> 00:09:52.955
See for yourself.

00:09:58.497 --> 00:10:01.955
Your child has
Cardassian DNA strands here

00:10:02.067 --> 00:10:04.558
and Kazon DNA here.

00:10:04.603 --> 00:10:09.540
Human DNA has a significantly
different nucleotide sequence.

00:10:10.876 --> 00:10:13.504
But I was so certain.
He looks...

00:10:13.545 --> 00:10:16.275
He's the first offspring
of a Cardassian and a Kazon.

00:10:16.315 --> 00:10:17.748
We have no frame of reference

00:10:17.783 --> 00:10:20.274
by which to judge
his initial appearance.

00:10:20.319 --> 00:10:22.719
Perhaps he will develop
more Kazon features

00:10:22.754 --> 00:10:24.244
as he matures.

00:10:24.289 --> 00:10:27.258
Maje Culluh will be so pleased.

00:10:27.292 --> 00:10:30.159
End medical holographic program.

00:10:36.902 --> 00:10:39.735
Medical Log, Stardate 50032.7.

00:10:39.771 --> 00:10:41.671
I have determined
that Commander Chakotay

00:10:41.707 --> 00:10:43.368
is not the father
of Seska's child.

00:10:43.408 --> 00:10:45.968
I only wish there was
some way to inform him.

00:10:47.412 --> 00:10:49.937
What am I supposed to do...

00:10:49.981 --> 00:10:52.950
lead a revolt
with the gang from Sandrine's?

00:10:52.984 --> 00:10:56.010
Conjure up holograms
of Nathan Hale and Che Guevara?

00:10:56.088 --> 00:10:58.147
I'm a Doctor,
not a counterinsurgent.

00:10:58.190 --> 00:11:00.624
Get ahold of yourself.

00:11:00.659 --> 00:11:02.149
You're not just a hologram.

00:11:02.194 --> 00:11:04.788
You're a Starfleet hologram.

00:11:06.832 --> 00:11:07.958
Maybe...

00:11:09.568 --> 00:11:12.867
maybe I could access
a tactical database...

00:11:12.904 --> 00:11:14.895
teach myself guerrilla warfare.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:17.272
But that would take time.

00:11:17.309 --> 00:11:19.971
Computer, what is
the crew complement?

00:11:20.011 --> 00:11:22.206
There are 89 Kazon...

00:11:22.247 --> 00:11:23.214
Eighty-nine...

00:11:23.248 --> 00:11:25.478
and one Betazoid on board.

00:11:25.517 --> 00:11:28.384
What did you say?
Betazoid?

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:30.911
There is one Betazoid on board.

00:11:30.956 --> 00:11:32.446
Where? Who?

00:11:32.491 --> 00:11:34.322
Please restate
a single question.

00:11:34.359 --> 00:11:35.792
Who is it?

00:11:35.827 --> 00:11:38.159
Crewman Lon Suder.

00:11:38.196 --> 00:11:39.993
Suder?

00:11:40.065 --> 00:11:41.555
Where is he?

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:43.932
Between Decks 8 and 9.

00:11:46.438 --> 00:11:47.928
Doctor to Suder.

00:11:47.973 --> 00:11:49.838
Yes.

00:11:49.875 --> 00:11:52.002
Yes, Doctor, I hear you.

00:11:52.077 --> 00:11:54.545
The ship has been taken over
by the Kazon-Nistrim.

00:11:56.314 --> 00:11:59.010
I know.
I've been hiding.

00:11:59.117 --> 00:12:01.551
Can you make it to Sick Bay?

00:12:01.586 --> 00:12:03.383
I think so.

00:12:04.689 --> 00:12:07.283
Computer, emergency
medical priority 1-1-4.

00:12:07.325 --> 00:12:08.849
Delete the signature
of Mr. Suder's combadge

00:12:08.894 --> 00:12:09.861
from the system.

00:12:09.895 --> 00:12:12.329
There is to be no record
of his being on board.

00:12:13.832 --> 00:12:15.231
Huddle together in groups.

00:12:15.267 --> 00:12:16.495
That'll preserve body heat.

00:12:16.535 --> 00:12:17.729
This is no time to be shy.

00:12:17.769 --> 00:12:18.736
Tuvok...

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:21.170
Captain, how do you
like your eggs?

00:12:21.206 --> 00:12:23.674
We found a nest
about two kilometers away.

00:12:23.708 --> 00:12:24.640
And that's not all...

00:12:24.676 --> 00:12:26.769
cucumbers,
or something like them.

00:12:26.812 --> 00:12:29.144
There are vines full of them
two hours from here.

00:12:29.181 --> 00:12:30.148
Take them to Neelix

00:12:30.182 --> 00:12:31.979
and tell him to hold off
on the beetle stew,

00:12:32.083 --> 00:12:33.675
at least for the time being.

00:12:37.189 --> 00:12:39.555
How's she doing, Samantha?

00:12:39.591 --> 00:12:40.888
I don't know, Captain.

00:12:40.926 --> 00:12:42.621
She seems tired, listless.

00:12:42.661 --> 00:12:44.720
Maybe she's just adjusting
to the environment.

00:12:44.763 --> 00:12:47.129
After all,
she was born in space.

00:12:47.165 --> 00:12:49.690
Make sure you
stay close to the fire...

00:12:49.734 --> 00:12:52.100
as soon as we have one.

00:13:02.247 --> 00:13:03.407
Trapped on a barren planet

00:13:03.448 --> 00:13:05.473
and you're stuck with the
only Indian in the universe

00:13:05.517 --> 00:13:08.452
who can't start a fire by
rubbing two sticks together.

00:13:08.487 --> 00:13:10.216
I was never good
at this as a child

00:13:10.255 --> 00:13:11.745
and I'm still not good at it.

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:12.950
Don't be so hard on yourself.

00:13:12.991 --> 00:13:14.515
None of the others have had
any success with it either.

00:13:14.559 --> 00:13:15.526
Must be the wood.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:17.790
We need kindling of some sort.

00:13:20.398 --> 00:13:22.298
What?

00:13:22.334 --> 00:13:25.633
Something my father once told
me about starting a fire.

00:13:37.282 --> 00:13:38.681
There you go.

00:14:03.141 --> 00:14:05.769
If we put some bigger
rocks around the fire,

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:07.402
they'll reflect the heat better.

00:14:07.445 --> 00:14:08.969
I'm going to go get some.

00:14:26.331 --> 00:14:27.855
Neelix.

00:14:30.335 --> 00:14:33.202
You shouldn't go
too far away from camp.

00:14:47.986 --> 00:14:49.954
Voyager's been taken
by the Kazon-Nistrim.

00:14:49.988 --> 00:14:52.923
They're flooding every subspace
frequency with the news.

00:14:52.958 --> 00:14:55.153
Is there any word on the crew?

00:14:55.193 --> 00:14:56.820
I'm afraid not.

00:15:00.465 --> 00:15:01.693
If you can help me with repairs,

00:15:01.733 --> 00:15:03.098
we can be on our way
in a few hours.

00:15:03.134 --> 00:15:04.328
Lieutenant...

00:15:04.369 --> 00:15:06.633
our ships are
no match for Voyager

00:15:06.671 --> 00:15:08.070
and your shuttlecraft
can hardly be...

00:15:08.106 --> 00:15:11.564
Commander Paxim,
my people are counting on you.

00:15:12.777 --> 00:15:15.473
Look, no one knows Voyager
like I do.

00:15:15.513 --> 00:15:18.175
I know every vulnerability,
every blind spot.

00:15:18.216 --> 00:15:20.207
Don't worry.
I have a plan.

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:23.082
Very well.

00:15:23.121 --> 00:15:24.952
We'll rendezvous in an hour.

00:15:25.056 --> 00:15:27.149
Paxim out.

00:15:28.893 --> 00:15:30.554
One hour.

00:15:30.595 --> 00:15:33.257
I should be able to come up
with some kind of plan

00:15:33.298 --> 00:15:34.663
in one hour.

00:15:46.077 --> 00:15:47.772
I was beginning to think
you'd gotten lost.

00:15:47.812 --> 00:15:49.245
I'm sorry.

00:15:49.280 --> 00:15:51.180
They're still
repairing the ship.

00:15:52.183 --> 00:15:53.775
I had to be careful.

00:15:53.818 --> 00:15:55.217
We have no time to waste.

00:15:55.253 --> 00:15:56.481
According to the computer,
we're at warp.

00:15:56.521 --> 00:15:58.216
We've got to figure out some way
to slow the ship down

00:15:58.256 --> 00:15:59.348
before we get too far
from the crew.

00:15:59.391 --> 00:16:00.915
That would seem to be
our first priority.

00:16:00.959 --> 00:16:02.654
And then we have
to get some weapons...

00:16:03.962 --> 00:16:07.227
Mr. Suder,
are you listening to me?

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:10.497
Yes.

00:16:10.535 --> 00:16:12.799
Oh.

00:16:12.837 --> 00:16:15.431
I see.

00:16:15.473 --> 00:16:18.840
Perhaps you consider this...
an opportunity.

00:16:20.178 --> 00:16:21.236
Opportunity?

00:16:21.279 --> 00:16:23.770
To obtain your freedom
from confinement.

00:16:23.815 --> 00:16:26.147
How foolish of me to think
you would want to help.

00:16:26.184 --> 00:16:27.617
You're wrong.

00:16:27.652 --> 00:16:30.314
I do want to help.

00:16:30.355 --> 00:16:32.915
Then... what?

00:16:40.265 --> 00:16:42.733
I'm going to have
to kill some of them.

00:16:42.767 --> 00:16:45.600
It is possible.

00:16:45.637 --> 00:16:49.300
Violence might be required
to retake the ship.

00:16:50.909 --> 00:16:52.900
I've worked so...

00:16:52.944 --> 00:16:57.074
so hard over
the last few months...

00:16:57.115 --> 00:16:59.845
to control the violent feelings.

00:16:59.884 --> 00:17:03.650
I'm almost at peace with myself.

00:17:03.688 --> 00:17:07.558
I mean, I see the day coming
when I could be.

00:17:08.625 --> 00:17:10.616
Mr. Suder...

00:17:10.661 --> 00:17:11.923
if Lieutenant Tuvok were here,

00:17:11.962 --> 00:17:14.089
I know he would tell you
there are times

00:17:14.131 --> 00:17:16.895
when violence is required
to defend yourself,

00:17:16.934 --> 00:17:20.199
to defend your ship,
to defend your crew.

00:17:20.237 --> 00:17:22.171
Yes.

00:17:22.205 --> 00:17:27.837
There is a logical use
for violence for everyone else.

00:17:27.878 --> 00:17:30.938
With me, once it begins...

00:17:30.981 --> 00:17:33.040
We must do this together,
Mr. Suder.

00:17:33.083 --> 00:17:35.574
If you don't trust yourself yet,

00:17:35.619 --> 00:17:36.745
then trust me.

00:17:36.787 --> 00:17:39.085
I will help you any way I can.

00:17:39.122 --> 00:17:40.885
One hologram and one sociopath

00:17:40.924 --> 00:17:43.392
may not be much
of a match for the Kazon,

00:17:43.427 --> 00:17:45.588
but... we'll have to do.

00:17:47.731 --> 00:17:49.596
There are signs of a struggle
near the edge of camp.

00:17:49.633 --> 00:17:51.760
I found alien tracks.

00:17:51.802 --> 00:17:54.168
We can't wait until
morning to go after them.

00:17:54.204 --> 00:17:56.570
Well, I'm better at tracking
than starting fires.

00:17:56.607 --> 00:17:57.699
I've completed a few weapons

00:17:57.741 --> 00:17:59.231
that might be appropriate,
Commander.

00:18:00.844 --> 00:18:03.005
This is thoughtful of you,
Tuvok.

00:18:03.046 --> 00:18:05.071
But my tribe never
used bows and arrows

00:18:05.115 --> 00:18:06.707
and I've never even shot one.

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:08.115
This is mine.

00:18:08.151 --> 00:18:10.051
I taught archery science
for several years

00:18:10.087 --> 00:18:12.817
at the Vulcan Institute
of Defensive Arts.

00:18:12.856 --> 00:18:14.983
Take as many crew
members as you need.

00:18:41.652 --> 00:18:43.449
Tus.

00:18:43.487 --> 00:18:45.318
Filhin hissen.

00:18:45.355 --> 00:18:46.549
Now, see here.

00:18:46.590 --> 00:18:48.820
You just keep
your hands off her.

00:18:49.826 --> 00:18:51.418
Toru hin!

00:18:51.461 --> 00:18:53.827
Dart hin cahi. Filhir.

00:18:55.632 --> 00:18:58.328
Tirk hir pahin!

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:11.047
Shod!

00:19:11.081 --> 00:19:12.912
Kuwissu hir. Shod!

00:19:13.016 --> 00:19:14.244
Commander, thank goodness.

00:19:14.284 --> 00:19:15.251
Are you all right?

00:19:15.285 --> 00:19:16.718
They haven't hurt us.

00:19:16.753 --> 00:19:18.812
Have you been able to tell
if they have a leader?

00:19:18.855 --> 00:19:20.550
I'd say it's the one
with the claw.

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:21.579
I agree.

00:19:21.625 --> 00:19:24.355
The other two seem to be
trying to figure out

00:19:24.394 --> 00:19:25.918
what to make of us.

00:19:25.962 --> 00:19:28.863
In a manner of speaking, not
in a culinary sense, I hope.

00:19:32.202 --> 00:19:33.601
Listen to the sound of my voice

00:19:33.637 --> 00:19:36.629
and you'll know
that I mean you no harm.

00:19:36.673 --> 00:19:38.607
I come without weapons.

00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:41.905
But I must have my people back.

00:19:41.945 --> 00:19:43.071
Shod!

00:19:43.113 --> 00:19:44.080
Kuwissu hir!

00:19:44.114 --> 00:19:45.638
Toru hin!

00:19:45.682 --> 00:19:47.172
Toru hin!

00:19:47.217 --> 00:19:48.878
Lam!

00:19:48.919 --> 00:19:51.945
Tolun...

00:19:51.988 --> 00:19:54.354
kusettun hatru.

00:20:07.771 --> 00:20:09.432
Thank you...

00:20:09.473 --> 00:20:11.134
but she should stay with you.

00:20:11.174 --> 00:20:13.142
I must take them with me.

00:20:13.176 --> 00:20:14.143
Korto!

00:20:14.177 --> 00:20:15.974
Korido koti hin!

00:20:16.046 --> 00:20:18.947
Dert hissen sahk!

00:20:20.317 --> 00:20:23.582
Stand? Certainly,
I'll be happy to stand.

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:25.747
Over here. Fine.

00:20:25.789 --> 00:20:28.223
Chim kan issen sahk.

00:20:28.258 --> 00:20:29.225
What?

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:31.124
No. No.

00:20:31.161 --> 00:20:33.527
No! That is unacceptable.

00:20:34.564 --> 00:20:36.361
Kes, stand up slowly

00:20:36.399 --> 00:20:38.765
and walk away with us.

00:20:47.110 --> 00:20:49.635
We have to go now.

00:20:50.747 --> 00:20:53.375
Kuharin. Tectisin!

00:20:53.416 --> 00:20:55.247
Just keep walking.
Don't look back.

00:20:55.285 --> 00:20:56.912
Kha hin!

00:21:17.808 --> 00:21:19.400
In there!

00:21:19.442 --> 00:21:22.343
Commander, that looks just
like the tunnel where Hogan...

00:21:22.379 --> 00:21:24.609
I know. If they know it, too,
they won't follow us in.

00:21:24.648 --> 00:21:26.206
Come on!

00:21:56.446 --> 00:21:57.811
You'd think this crew

00:21:57.848 --> 00:22:00.510
had never seen
a warp drive before.

00:22:00.550 --> 00:22:03.144
No one tried to adjust
the antimatter flow today?

00:22:03.186 --> 00:22:05.484
No one.

00:22:05.522 --> 00:22:08.457
If you're lying,
I'll have your head.

00:22:08.491 --> 00:22:10.516
I swear it, Maje.

00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:11.857
There should have
been some warning

00:22:11.895 --> 00:22:13.954
before the antimatter
injector froze...

00:22:14.030 --> 00:22:17.397
a drop in core temperature,
a magnetic constriction alarm...

00:22:17.434 --> 00:22:18.594
something.

00:22:18.635 --> 00:22:21.229
He's either lying or...

00:22:21.271 --> 00:22:23.739
Or what?

00:22:23.773 --> 00:22:27.140
Computer, run a level-1
scan for intruders.

00:22:27.177 --> 00:22:28.804
Unable to comply.

00:22:28.845 --> 00:22:31.609
Internal scanner relays
have been damaged.

00:22:31.648 --> 00:22:34.344
I thought you said all
repairs were complete.

00:22:34.384 --> 00:22:35.442
They were.

00:22:35.485 --> 00:22:37.214
I thought they were.

00:22:37.254 --> 00:22:39.916
I want a deck-by-deck search

00:22:39.956 --> 00:22:41.787
of all Jefferies tubes
and conduits.

00:22:41.825 --> 00:22:44.191
Use the Federation tricorders.

00:22:44.227 --> 00:22:47.458
Do you have a portable
thoron generator?

00:22:47.497 --> 00:22:49.192
Yes, of course.

00:22:49.232 --> 00:22:51.257
We use it to treat
radiation burns.

00:22:51.301 --> 00:22:53.462
It's an old Maquis trick.

00:22:53.503 --> 00:22:56.870
Thoron particles neutralize
tricorder sensors.

00:22:58.675 --> 00:23:00.802
Mr. Suder, we need some weapons

00:23:00.844 --> 00:23:03.278
if we're going
to retake the ship.

00:23:13.924 --> 00:23:15.619
She has a fever.

00:23:15.659 --> 00:23:17.126
I don't know what to do.

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:19.151
Let me get her some water.

00:23:27.804 --> 00:23:29.965
The baby needs water.

00:23:30.040 --> 00:23:31.974
Those tremors seem
to be getting stronger.

00:23:32.042 --> 00:23:34.169
Chakotay's team should
have been back by now.

00:23:34.210 --> 00:23:35.802
We better look for them
before it gets too hot.

00:23:35.845 --> 00:23:36.869
Get a few people together.

00:23:36.913 --> 00:23:37.971
I'll join you in a second.

00:23:48.124 --> 00:23:49.216
Come on.

00:23:49.259 --> 00:23:51.090
We have to see if there's
another way out of here.

00:24:32.836 --> 00:24:34.804
I feel a breeze.

00:24:34.838 --> 00:24:37.170
It's coming from this way.

00:25:17.147 --> 00:25:19.047
Do you really think Commander
Chakotay would go in there

00:25:19.082 --> 00:25:20.071
after what happened
to Hogan?

00:25:20.116 --> 00:25:21.515
He may have had
no other choice.

00:25:21.551 --> 00:25:23.485
How do we get them
away from the tunnels?

00:25:23.520 --> 00:25:24.646
A couple of phaser blasts
would do the trick.

00:25:24.687 --> 00:25:26.621
Who are the fastest runners
here?

00:25:26.656 --> 00:25:29.420
I was on the decathlon team
before I quit the Academy.

00:25:29.459 --> 00:25:31.791
The track and field coach
was furious with me.

00:25:31.828 --> 00:25:33.352
Anyone else here who can run?

00:25:33.396 --> 00:25:34.385
Yeah.

00:25:34.431 --> 00:25:36.729
Okay, you three will
be the sprint team.

00:25:36.766 --> 00:25:38.666
Once you reach our camp,
you should be safe.

00:25:39.803 --> 00:25:41.327
Which way do you like, Tuvok?

00:25:41.371 --> 00:25:45.501
From a tactical point of view,
the options are not encouraging.

00:25:45.542 --> 00:25:47.373
However, moving past
the creature

00:25:47.410 --> 00:25:49.139
might lead us to an exit.

00:25:49.179 --> 00:25:51.079
All right, let's take it slow.

00:25:51.114 --> 00:25:52.445
Single file.

00:26:08.164 --> 00:26:10.132
Hey, up here!

00:26:10.166 --> 00:26:11.633
- Come on!
- Up here! You want us?

00:26:11.668 --> 00:26:14.262
You want us,
come and get us.

00:26:14.304 --> 00:26:16.636
Come on, come and get us.

00:26:35.724 --> 00:26:36.850
Pull this.

00:26:56.145 --> 00:26:57.476
Look out!

00:27:08.624 --> 00:27:09.682
Chakotay!

00:27:09.725 --> 00:27:10.714
Tuvok!

00:27:13.162 --> 00:27:14.129
The tunnel is clear.

00:27:14.163 --> 00:27:14.959
Go!

00:27:25.941 --> 00:27:27.067
Everybody out!

00:27:31.580 --> 00:27:32.945
Move! Let's go!

00:27:33.048 --> 00:27:34.310
Go! Go! Go!

00:27:34.349 --> 00:27:35.338
Go!

00:27:38.253 --> 00:27:39.311
Chakotay, a spear.

00:27:53.302 --> 00:27:55.361
Go, go, go!

00:27:55.404 --> 00:27:57.235
Come on, come on, go.

00:28:03.212 --> 00:28:04.702
Come on.

00:28:09.618 --> 00:28:11.552
I don't understand it.

00:28:11.587 --> 00:28:13.282
Thoron particles are leaking

00:28:13.322 --> 00:28:15.313
into the conduits
from somewhere.

00:28:15.357 --> 00:28:17.552
I can't get any other readings.

00:28:17.593 --> 00:28:18.582
Check the next level.

00:28:18.627 --> 00:28:19.651
Yes, sir.

00:28:50.759 --> 00:28:52.590
Incoming subspace message

00:28:52.628 --> 00:28:55.188
on the emergency medical
holographic channel.

00:28:55.230 --> 00:28:56.959
On the emergency channel?

00:28:57.065 --> 00:28:59.727
Doc, I hope you're
receiving this

00:28:59.768 --> 00:29:01.759
because if you're not,
I'm a dead duck.

00:29:01.803 --> 00:29:04.465
I'm piggy-backing this message
on a fake Kazon signal

00:29:04.506 --> 00:29:06.030
I'm sending to the Bridge.

00:29:06.074 --> 00:29:07.166
I'm betting they won't be

00:29:07.209 --> 00:29:09.336
monitoring
your emergency medical channel.

00:29:09.378 --> 00:29:11.778
I'm bringing help.

00:29:11.813 --> 00:29:13.508
But you have
to do something for us.

00:29:13.548 --> 00:29:16.483
When the attack begins,
I need you to get

00:29:16.518 --> 00:29:17.917
the computer
to block the discharge

00:29:17.953 --> 00:29:20.183
from the backup
phaser power couplings.

00:29:20.222 --> 00:29:21.348
You got that?

00:29:21.390 --> 00:29:22.880
The backup couplings.

00:29:22.924 --> 00:29:25.358
I'm taking out
the primary couplings myself,

00:29:25.394 --> 00:29:27.225
but I need those backups
to overload

00:29:27.262 --> 00:29:28.627
when they switch to them.

00:29:28.664 --> 00:29:31.565
Don't do anything
until the attack begins

00:29:31.600 --> 00:29:32.794
or they might notice.

00:29:32.834 --> 00:29:34.563
That's it for now.

00:29:34.603 --> 00:29:35.865
I'll be seeing you soon.

00:29:35.904 --> 00:29:37.872
I hope.

00:29:45.347 --> 00:29:46.405
Good news.

00:29:46.448 --> 00:29:47.574
Help is on the way.

00:29:47.616 --> 00:29:49.083
Mr. Paris apparently
was able to...

00:29:51.720 --> 00:29:52.948
Oh.

00:29:53.021 --> 00:29:54.545
I didn't know what to do.

00:29:54.589 --> 00:29:56.079
I didn't think
I should leave him there

00:29:56.124 --> 00:29:57.182
where they could find him.

00:29:57.225 --> 00:29:59.125
Of course. You were smart
to bring him here.

00:29:59.161 --> 00:30:01.322
We can put him
in a stasis drawer.

00:30:01.363 --> 00:30:04.924
Well, we have weapons now.

00:30:07.769 --> 00:30:10.738
You did what was
necessary, Mr. Suder.

00:30:12.708 --> 00:30:14.539
Five cc's of improvoline
will help you calm down.

00:30:14.576 --> 00:30:15.543
No.

00:30:15.577 --> 00:30:17.169
No drugs.

00:30:17.212 --> 00:30:19.237
I just need to breathe...

00:30:19.281 --> 00:30:22.182
see the light that is my breath.

00:30:30.692 --> 00:30:33.160
We just received a message
from our patrol ship.

00:30:34.863 --> 00:30:38.094
They've tracked down
the shuttle from Voyager...

00:30:38.133 --> 00:30:40.499
and destroyed it.

00:30:40.535 --> 00:30:42.366
Were two people on board?

00:30:42.404 --> 00:30:44.338
They didn't say.

00:30:44.373 --> 00:30:48.207
Two people were unaccounted for
when we captured the crew.

00:30:48.243 --> 00:30:51.872
Have they found any evidence
of an intruder on board?

00:30:51.913 --> 00:30:53.244
No.

00:30:53.281 --> 00:30:55.841
But the search
has been slowed down

00:30:55.884 --> 00:30:57.317
by a thoron particle leak.

00:30:57.352 --> 00:30:58.944
Thoron particles?

00:30:58.987 --> 00:31:02.081
That's an old Maquis trick
to fool tricorders.

00:31:04.426 --> 00:31:05.825
After what transpired,

00:31:05.861 --> 00:31:07.726
I believe we have
to prepare ourselves

00:31:07.763 --> 00:31:09.754
for an alien attack, Captain.

00:31:09.798 --> 00:31:11.425
Our priority should
be to increase

00:31:11.466 --> 00:31:12.899
the weapons arsenal,
and to begin

00:31:12.934 --> 00:31:14.959
training everyone
in the use of these weapons.

00:31:15.036 --> 00:31:16.799
I don't like the sound of that,
Lieutenant.

00:31:16.838 --> 00:31:19.671
We may have to coexist
with these aliens a long time.

00:31:19.708 --> 00:31:20.675
Nevertheless.

00:31:20.709 --> 00:31:21.733
I agree with the Captain.

00:31:21.777 --> 00:31:22.744
We have to find a way

00:31:22.778 --> 00:31:24.143
to share this world with them.

00:31:24.179 --> 00:31:26.739
You may find nobility
in the savage, Commander,

00:31:26.782 --> 00:31:28.977
but he is only interested
in killing you.

00:31:29.084 --> 00:31:30.483
I don't believe that.

00:31:30.519 --> 00:31:32.646
Captain!

00:31:32.687 --> 00:31:34.154
The baby is very sick.

00:31:34.189 --> 00:31:36.316
She's having trouble breathing.

00:31:36.358 --> 00:31:37.382
She has a high fever.

00:31:37.426 --> 00:31:39.860
There's nothing more
I can do for her.

00:31:39.895 --> 00:31:41.123
Captain!

00:31:45.500 --> 00:31:48.230
I think our top priority
has just been dictated.

00:31:48.270 --> 00:31:49.237
Break camp.

00:31:49.271 --> 00:31:50.966
We've got to get out
of here before it blows.

00:31:54.242 --> 00:31:55.607
Why are you still here?

00:31:55.644 --> 00:31:57.839
I shut down your
program when I left.

00:31:57.879 --> 00:31:59.870
You must be mistaken.

00:32:00.949 --> 00:32:03.042
Where's your thoron generator?

00:32:03.084 --> 00:32:05.780
It was damaged
on a recent away mission

00:32:05.821 --> 00:32:07.413
and left behind.

00:32:07.456 --> 00:32:10.050
Who else from Voyager
is on board?

00:32:10.091 --> 00:32:11.058
I wouldn't know.

00:32:11.092 --> 00:32:12.184
I don't believe you.

00:32:14.696 --> 00:32:17.130
There are several dozen
crewmen on board actually,

00:32:17.165 --> 00:32:18.598
and they have been
working 'round the clock

00:32:18.633 --> 00:32:19.600
to sabotage your vessel.

00:32:19.634 --> 00:32:21.192
That's a lie.

00:32:21.236 --> 00:32:22.601
At most, there is one

00:32:22.637 --> 00:32:24.229
and I believe
it is a Maquis crewman.

00:32:25.340 --> 00:32:26.602
Yes, of course.
You're right.

00:32:26.641 --> 00:32:27.733
It is one of the Maquis.

00:32:27.776 --> 00:32:30.438
I won't play these games
with a trick of light.

00:32:30.479 --> 00:32:32.208
Sticks and stones
won't break my bones,

00:32:32.247 --> 00:32:34.772
so you can imagine how I feel
about being called names.

00:32:36.017 --> 00:32:38.679
I don't believe you could
have sabotaged this ship alone.

00:32:40.956 --> 00:32:42.321
Very well.

00:32:42.357 --> 00:32:44.655
Since you are obviously about
to disable my program anyway,

00:32:44.693 --> 00:32:46.490
let me take
the credit I deserve.

00:32:46.528 --> 00:32:49.463
I did sabotage the ship
all by myself

00:32:49.498 --> 00:32:51.693
with the computer's
help, of course.

00:32:51.733 --> 00:32:52.757
As a matter of fact,

00:32:52.801 --> 00:32:54.826
one of your crewmen
came in unexpectedly

00:32:54.870 --> 00:32:56.235
and caught me in the act.

00:33:00.375 --> 00:33:01.637
You killed him?

00:33:01.676 --> 00:33:03.576
He left me no choice.

00:33:03.612 --> 00:33:06.410
Why create a thoron leak
if you're not hiding someone?

00:33:06.448 --> 00:33:07.779
I would think it's obvious.

00:33:07.816 --> 00:33:10.216
To make you believe
I was hiding someone.

00:33:10.252 --> 00:33:12.447
I've had your people
crawling through the bowels

00:33:12.487 --> 00:33:14.955
of this ship for hours,
looking for an intruder.

00:33:14.990 --> 00:33:16.855
You're more talented
in the art of deception

00:33:16.892 --> 00:33:18.052
than you led me to believe.

00:33:18.093 --> 00:33:21.187
I was inspired
by the presence of a master.

00:33:22.564 --> 00:33:24.725
Computer, access Culluh-0-1.

00:33:24.766 --> 00:33:27.234
Disregard all voice commands
from Starfleet personnel.

00:33:27.269 --> 00:33:29.066
Security lockout.

00:33:30.205 --> 00:33:32.605
Seska to Bridge.
What's going on?

00:33:32.641 --> 00:33:34.973
A couple of Talaxian ships
have fired on us.

00:33:35.043 --> 00:33:37.307
Nothing to worry about.

00:33:38.046 --> 00:33:40.276
Good-bye, Doctor.

00:33:40.315 --> 00:33:43.478
I'd rather not take
any more chances.

00:34:25.193 --> 00:34:26.455
Doctor?

00:34:34.335 --> 00:34:37.634
Activate emergency
medical holographic program.

00:34:37.672 --> 00:34:39.333
Unable to respond.

00:34:39.374 --> 00:34:42.502
All Starfleet voice access
has been canceled.

00:34:45.680 --> 00:34:49.480
Mr. Suder, if you
are hearing this,

00:34:49.517 --> 00:34:51.314
you have just
unsuccessfully attempted

00:34:51.352 --> 00:34:53.320
to access the emergency
medical program.

00:34:53.354 --> 00:34:54.981
I have programmed
this message to play

00:34:55.089 --> 00:34:56.852
in the event
that I have been disabled.

00:34:56.891 --> 00:34:58.518
This means, of course,
that the fate of Voyager

00:34:58.559 --> 00:35:01.460
now depends solely on you.

00:35:01.496 --> 00:35:03.760
I can imagine how you
must feel at this moment.

00:35:03.798 --> 00:35:06.733
I want you to know
you have my full confidence.

00:35:06.768 --> 00:35:08.793
You have already shown
great courage and dedication

00:35:08.836 --> 00:35:10.201
to your crew.

00:35:10.238 --> 00:35:11.500
I have left
an additional message

00:35:11.539 --> 00:35:13.131
for Captain Janeway
and Lieutenant Tuvok

00:35:13.174 --> 00:35:17.838
noting your heroism
in case I am... irretrievable.

00:35:17.879 --> 00:35:21.872
You know what you have to do
and when to do it.

00:35:21.916 --> 00:35:24.077
And I know that,
with our fate in your hands,

00:35:24.118 --> 00:35:25.517
we will prevail.

00:35:25.553 --> 00:35:28.044
Good luck, Mr. Suder.

00:35:53.014 --> 00:35:55.847
The Talaxians are retreating
toward the nebula.

00:35:55.883 --> 00:35:59.375
We'll teach them the price
for attacking the Nistrim.

00:35:59.420 --> 00:36:00.887
Lay in a pursuit course.

00:36:01.889 --> 00:36:03.447
Commander Paxim to Paris.

00:36:03.491 --> 00:36:04.890
Go ahead.

00:36:04.926 --> 00:36:06.291
They're following us as planned.

00:36:06.327 --> 00:36:07.692
We're bringing them to you.

00:36:07.729 --> 00:36:09.856
Acknowledged.
Ready and waiting.

00:36:09.897 --> 00:36:13.424
I just hope you are, too, Doc.

00:36:21.509 --> 00:36:23.170
This way.

00:36:39.627 --> 00:36:41.492
Chaka hu!

00:36:43.498 --> 00:36:46.524
Hahaki! Hahaki!

00:37:08.823 --> 00:37:10.848
It's okay.

00:37:45.827 --> 00:37:47.317
Tal karok.

00:38:00.608 --> 00:38:02.667
Here we go.

00:38:12.220 --> 00:38:13.847
What's happening?!

00:38:13.888 --> 00:38:16.789
Our phaser power couplings
are under attack.

00:38:16.824 --> 00:38:17.813
From where?

00:38:17.859 --> 00:38:19.087
I don't see anyone.

00:38:19.127 --> 00:38:21.322
I'm not picking up anything
on the scanners.

00:38:21.362 --> 00:38:21.919
Shields are buckling.

00:38:21.963 --> 00:38:24.158
Take evasive action.

00:39:48.349 --> 00:39:49.816
I have it on the scanners.

00:39:49.850 --> 00:39:52.045
It's a Federation shuttlecraft.

00:39:54.822 --> 00:39:57.791
Lock phasers.

00:39:57.825 --> 00:39:59.315
Destroy it.

00:39:59.360 --> 00:40:00.952
Primary phaser power is down.

00:40:01.996 --> 00:40:03.395
Switch to backup systems.

00:40:03.431 --> 00:40:04.955
Confirmed.

00:40:04.999 --> 00:40:06.967
Phasers are locked on.

00:40:07.001 --> 00:40:09.595
Fire!

00:40:13.708 --> 00:40:15.141
I don't understand.

00:40:15.176 --> 00:40:17.701
I'm showing an overload.

00:40:21.115 --> 00:40:23.549
Yes, Doc, yes.

00:40:23.584 --> 00:40:25.313
Paris to Commander Paxim.

00:40:25.353 --> 00:40:26.411
Stand by.

00:40:26.454 --> 00:40:28.581
I'm going to start transporting
your people to Voyager.

00:40:28.623 --> 00:40:30.056
Standing by.

00:40:49.543 --> 00:40:50.908
Oh. Seska!

00:40:54.615 --> 00:40:56.207
Seska!

00:41:16.937 --> 00:41:18.097
Seska...

00:41:34.522 --> 00:41:36.080
Engineering to Maje Culluh.

00:41:36.123 --> 00:41:37.590
We're being boarded.

00:41:37.625 --> 00:41:40.025
Abandon ship.

00:41:55.476 --> 00:41:57.603
I'm sealing off
the Bridge manually.

00:41:57.645 --> 00:41:59.545
I've got to get
the computer back on line.

00:42:00.548 --> 00:42:03.312
All Starfleet voice access
has been disabled.

00:42:03.351 --> 00:42:05.842
I'm reading a Kazon shuttle
leaving the ship.

00:42:05.886 --> 00:42:07.444
There are also escape
pods being launched.

00:42:07.488 --> 00:42:08.455
Forget them.

00:42:08.489 --> 00:42:10.320
We have more important
things to do.

00:42:37.451 --> 00:42:39.078
She's breathing
better, isn't she?

00:42:41.589 --> 00:42:43.819
Sod katok.

00:42:52.865 --> 00:42:55.197
Hanuk.
Hanuk!

00:42:55.234 --> 00:42:58.203
Hanuk! Hanuk!

00:43:00.806 --> 00:43:02.137
There.

00:43:25.865 --> 00:43:27.696
Welcome back, Captain.

00:43:31.871 --> 00:43:33.395
Well done, Lieutenant.

00:43:33.439 --> 00:43:34.463
I had a lot of help...

00:43:34.507 --> 00:43:36.975
the Talaxians,
the Doc, Mr. Suder.

00:43:37.009 --> 00:43:38.203
Suder?

00:43:38.244 --> 00:43:40.508
We thought he was killed
during the initial attack.

00:43:40.546 --> 00:43:43.606
No. He and the Doctor
sabotaged the ship.

00:43:43.649 --> 00:43:46.709
Suder disabled the phasers
before they killed him.

00:43:52.224 --> 00:43:55.193
You would have been
proud of him, Mr. Tuvok.

00:43:55.227 --> 00:43:58.958
I offer you
a Vulcan prayer, Mr. Suder.

00:44:01.167 --> 00:44:03.692
May your death
bring you the peace

00:44:03.736 --> 00:44:05.636
you never found in life.

00:44:28.360 --> 00:44:29.827
Mr. Kim,

00:44:29.862 --> 00:44:32.092
is this ship capable
of sustained flight?

00:44:32.131 --> 00:44:33.962
All propulsion
and navigational systems

00:44:34.066 --> 00:44:36.899
are functioning within normal
parameters, Captain.

00:44:36.936 --> 00:44:39.734
Good. Take us away
from our new home

00:44:39.772 --> 00:44:42.707
and set a course for
the old one, Mr. Paris, warp 8.

00:44:42.741 --> 00:44:46.507
Heading 41 mark 77.

00:44:46.545 --> 00:44:49.378
Destination: Alpha Quadrant.

00:44:53.819 --> 00:44:55.286
Engage.
